WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.576
In the year 923, Li Cunxu proclaimed himself emperor at Weizhou and founded Later Tang, then marched south and destroyed Later Liang in one stroke.

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:13.694
Banners streamed and the troops stood in perfect order.

00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:24.100
Li Cunxu was young and brave; he had campaigned with his father since childhood and was famed throughout the land for his skill in war — a born warrior.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.402
The soldiers marched with even steps.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:35.936
Kaifeng, the Later Liang capital, was captured, and the Later Liang dynasty, which had lasted only sixteen years, perished.

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:44.854
Li Cunxu ascended the throne full of spirit, determined to govern the country well and create a prosperous age.

00:00:45.204 --> 00:00:52.380
But gradually he favoured court actors and pushed away his meritorious officials, and disputes arose at court.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:59.810
Later Tang soon fell into new political conflict, and the Central Plains were once again in turmoil.

